.TH FGETC 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
fgetc \- read one byte from a Crunch stream
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <stdio.h>
.PP
.BI "int fgetc(struct FILE* " stream ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads one byte from the stream. The stream is unbuffered.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the byte as an integer from 0 to 255, or
.B EOF
(\-1) on end-of-file or error. Use
.BR feof (3crunch)
and
.BR ferror (3crunch)
to distinguish them. A null stream returns
.B EOF
with
.B errno
set to
.BR EINVAL .
.SH NOTES
Only Crunch streams are supported; they are not C library
.B FILE
objects.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fputc (3crunch),
.BR fread (3crunch),
.BR stdin (3crunch)
